.TH SDL_GetRelativeMouseState 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetRelativeMouseState \- Query SDL\(aqs cache for the synchronous mouse button state and accumulated mouse delta since last call.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_mouse.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_MouseButtonFlags SDL_GetRelativeMouseState(float *x, float *y);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function returns the cached synchronous state as SDL understands it from the last pump of the event queue\[char46]
.PP
To query the platform for immediate asynchronous state, use
.BR SDL_GetGlobalMouseState \[char46]
.PP
Passing non-NULL pointers to
.BR x
or
.BR y
will write the destination with respective x or y deltas accumulated since the last call to this function (or since event initialization)\[char46]
.PP
This function is useful for reducing overhead by processing relative mouse inputs in one go per-frame instead of individually per-event, at the expense of losing the order between events within the frame (e\[char46]g\[char46] quickly pressing and releasing a button within the same frame)\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I x
a pointer to receive the x mouse delta accumulated since last call, can be NULL if unused\[char46]
.TP
.I y
a pointer to receive the y mouse delta accumulated since last call, can be NULL if unused\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a 32-bit bitmask of the button state that can be bitwise-compared against the
.BR SDL_BUTTON_MASK (X)
macro\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetMouseState (3),
.BR SDL_GetGlobalMouseState (3)
